//BUG="an AutoRef nested directly inside another AutoRef is never resolved"
//OUT="7"

// Not in FEEDBACK.md, and not the same as 13-15: `grid[0][0]` parses fine, it
// aborts the compiler in codegen with
//
//     unreachable!("IRExpression::AutoRef should not be emitted by normalizer")
//
// The lowerer turns `x[i]` into `AutoRef(operator[](AutoRef(x) i))`, so a
// second index produces an AutoRef whose child is another AutoRef.
// `IRPass::pass_expression` (src/compiler/normalizer/ir_pass.rs) calls
// `pre_map_expression` once, at the top, and then dispatches on whatever came
// back. `CheckRefsPass::pre_map_expression` replaces an AutoRef of depth 0
// with its child unchanged — so the child, itself an AutoRef, is handed
// straight to the `IRExpression::AutoRef` match arm, which recurses into *its*
// child but never runs `pre_map_expression` on the node itself. The inner
// AutoRef survives the pass and reaches codegen.
//
// Depth 0 is what a vector of vectors produces: `Vec.operator[]` returns `&T`
// and the outer `operator[]` wants `&Vec`, so no reference has to be added.
// `grid[0].x` is fine because a field access forces a dereference (depth -1).
//
// The fix is for `pass_expression` to re-enter when `pre_map_expression`
// returns a different node kind, or for the pass to resolve the child first.

fn main
    grid = Vec[Vec[i32]]()
    row = Vec[i32]()
    row.push(7)
    grid.push(row)
    out "{grid[0][0]}"
